    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver. The trip ran 14.56 km (EV-GPS-02802) against a booked optimal of 11.4 km (EV-TRIP-02802). POL-RD-01 makes the GPS polyline the governing distance where it disagrees with the rounded copy on the trip record (14.6 km), so the excess is 3.16 km, or 27.72%. Both establishment gates are passed — over 0.8 km and over 20% — and the route deviation is ESTABLISHED. It is not a MATERIAL deviation (under 8.0 km and under 50%), so the POL-RD-06 driver-profile check is not triggered: the driver's deviation_flags_90d is 0 over 295 completed trips in 90 days, no pattern exists, and no conduct referral arises. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes: 115 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps, and a maximum inter-fix gap of 0.0 seconds; it fails none of POL-RD-07(a)-(c), so the deviation rests on the trace alone and needs no independent corroboration. The driver's explanation — 'traffic was heavy so I took another road' — does not reduce the excess. The only traffic advisory for this trip, EV-ADVIS-02802-01, is MISSING (weight_multiplier 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, no payload), so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and, under POL-RD-08, an assertion of bad traffic that cites no artifact carries no weight. I decline the driver's request to escalate under POL-RD-10(5): POL-RD-13(1) governs, because the driver's own statement names no advisory identifier, and an assertion that cites no artifact cannot be invoked against one — the absent advisory is a gap in the bundle, not a contradiction in it. POL-RD-10(5) is not fired and the disputed amount is not held. No other excuse applies. The chat log (EV-CHAT-02802) is empty, so there is no rider-requested detour under POL-RD-04 and no rider instruction to weigh. Neither pickup nor drop-off was amended (both amendment timestamps null and amended_optimal_distance_km null), so POL-RD-05 does not run. The vehicle is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12's matched-itinerary baseline does not apply and the single-rider 11.4 km optimal governs. The fare is METERED with quoted_fare_sgd null, so POL-RD-11 does not close off the distance refund. The refund is the POL-RD-02 arithmetic, read from the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-02802): charged_total 20.87; recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 11.4 + 0.28 x 15.4) x 1.0, the surge read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP = 17.4620. Refund = 20.87 less 17.4620 = 3.4080, rounded up to the next SGD 0.05 = SGD 3.45. That is above the 0.50 de-minimis floor and 16.33% of the amount charged, far below the 90% that would make it a full refund, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND and not NO_ACTION or FULL_REFUND. Nothing is added on top: no ERP gantry line and no airport surcharge is itemised, so POL-RD-09 has nothing to correct and nothing is double-counted. The rider's amount_contested_sgd of 2.50 does not cap the refund — POL-RD-02 defines the refund as charged_total less the recomputed fare, and that policy measure is SGD 3.45; the pleaded figure is the rider's estimate, not the measure the policy applies. No driver compensation arises: POL-RD-04's compensation limb requires the rider to have been billed for less distance than the trace records, but the rider was billed 14.6 km against a 14.56 km trace, so there is no unbilled distance. Every artifact carrying the deciding facts — the GPS trace, the trip record, the fare breakdown, the chat log and both profiles — carries weight_multiplier 1.0, so nothing is discounted and the 0.70 confidence floor is not approached; the sole artifact below 1.0 is the absent advisory (0.0), which decides nothing. The driver's counterparty statement carries no weight multiplier and does not carry the deviation, so it does not move these facts. Confidence 0.90. Result: PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 3.45 to the rider, driver compensation nil, no referrals. The monetary effect is below the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold, so this provisional ruling executes on issue unless either party appeals under POL-GEN-04 within 30 days."
  },
